{
  "chapter": "patterns/scale/mapreduce-tree",
  "tier": "micro",
  "notes": [
    "Reduce in a tree rather than a single pass, so no reduce step ever sees more than",
    "`fanIn` inputs. Merging is left-to-right within a group, and groups are formed from",
    "adjacent items, which is what keeps the result order-preserving.",
    "`levels` records the tree, one entry per round of merging."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "a-single-item-needs-no-merging",
      "items": ["a"],
      "fanIn": 2,
      "result": { "result": "a", "levels": [] }
    },
    {
      "id": "a-full-group-merges-in-one-level",
      "items": ["a", "b"],
      "fanIn": 2,
      "result": { "result": "(a+b)", "levels": [["(a+b)"]] }
    },
    {
      "id": "an-odd-item-carries-to-the-next-level",
      "items": ["a", "b", "c"],
      "fanIn": 2,
      "result": { "result": "((a+b)+c)", "levels": [["(a+b)", "c"], ["((a+b)+c)"]] }
    },
    {
      "id": "four-items-balance-into-two-levels",
      "items": ["a", "b", "c", "d"],
      "fanIn": 2,
      "result": {
        "result": "((a+b)+(c+d))",
        "levels": [["(a+b)", "(c+d)"], ["((a+b)+(c+d))"]]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a-wider-fan-in-flattens-the-tree",
      "items": ["a", "b", "c", "d"],
      "fanIn": 4,
      "result": { "result": "(a+b+c+d)", "levels": [["(a+b+c+d)"]] }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-tree-deepens-as-the-input-grows",
      "items": ["a", "b", "c", "d", "e"],
      "fanIn": 2,
      "result": {
        "result": "(((a+b)+(c+d))+e)",
        "levels": [
          ["(a+b)", "(c+d)", "e"],
          ["((a+b)+(c+d))", "e"],
          ["(((a+b)+(c+d))+e)"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "no-items-reduce-to-nothing",
      "items": [],
      "fanIn": 2,
      "result": { "result": null, "levels": [] }
    }
  ]
}
